# LZMA and LZMA2 decompression, and the two files they travel in: the
# .xz container (The .xz File Format, version 1.0.4, Tukaani project,
# 2009-08-27, which 1.2.1 restates) and the legacy .lzma file that LZMA
# Utils and the LZMA SDK write (liblzma calls it LZMA_Alone). Written in
# iyi; no liblzma is linked. The decoder follows the shape of XZ
# Embedded's `xz_dec_lzma2.c` (Lasse Collin and Igor Pavlov, public
# domain): the range coder, the twelve-state machine, the probability
# tables and their layout are that file's, and so is the rule for the
# input - at least 21 bytes in hand before a symbol, the most one can
# take, or the rest of what there is - so a symbol is never begun and
# then left half-read when a piece of the stream runs out.
#
# `XzReader` reads a stream a piece at a time: the compressed bytes come
# from an IyiIO, the decompressed ones go out through `read`, as
# std/compress's `Inflater` does for DEFLATE. `Xz.decompress` is the same
# reader run over one string. A stream that is not what it says - a
# check, an index, a header CRC that does not match, a size the data does
# not have, LZMA data that is not LZMA, a stream that ends early - is an
# `XzError`, a value, the first sentence that saw it, and every read
# after it answers the same.
#
# What a .xz file holds is read and checked whole. Every block header's
# CRC32, its flags and its padding; its compressed and uncompressed sizes
# when it gives them, against what the block turned out to be; the
# block's padding, and its check - none, CRC32, CRC64 (std/digest's
# `CRC64`) or SHA-256, the four xz writes - over what was decompressed;
# the index, its record count, each record against the block it names
# (kept as liblzma keeps them, as counts and sums and a CRC-64 of the
# records, so a stream of a million blocks costs nothing per block), its
# padding and CRC32; and the stream footer against the header and the
# index. Streams may follow one another, with stream padding (zero bytes,
# a multiple of four) between and after them, as `xz` reads them; the
# check types the format reserves (2, 3, 5 to 9, 11 to 15) are refused by
# name rather than read unchecked. Bytes after the last stream that are
# neither padding nor another stream are refused too: `xz` refuses them,
# where Python's `lzma.decompress` drops them.
#
# The filters a block may name are LZMA2, which must be last, and before
# it the delta filter and the x86 branch-call-jump filter (BCJ, with or
# without its start offset), the two Python's `lzma` and `xz --delta`,
# `--x86` write for data that wants them; the other BCJ filters (PowerPC,
# IA-64, ARM, ARM-Thumb, SPARC, ARM64, RISC-V) are refused by name. A
# .lzma file is a 13-byte header - lc, lp and pb, the dictionary size and
# the uncompressed size or "unknown" - and one LZMA stream, ended by its
# size, by the end-of-payload marker, or by the size and then a marker,
# which XZ Utils' own test files hold good too; bytes after it are
# refused. A block header's sizes are held to as the block is read: a
# chunk that would take it past either is refused before it is decoded.
#
# Memory is the dictionary and what waits to be read, and the dictionary
# is the stream's own word for how far back it reaches: an LZMA2 filter's
# dictionary property, a .lzma header's size. One past the reader's
# `dict_limit` - 64 MiB unless the caller says otherwise, what `xz -9`
# writes - is refused before anything is allocated for it, so a stream
# cannot ask for more memory than the caller agreed to. Under it, the
# ring the dictionary lives in starts at 64 KiB and doubles as the output
# reaches it, so a kilobyte written with `xz -9e`'s 64 MiB dictionary
# allocated under 512 KiB in all (the gate measures it). The input is a
# buffer of 128 KiB that the pieces are copied through. Streamed 64 KiB
# a read, 64 MiB with an 8 MiB dictionary kept the collector under
# 12 MiB. Measured on one x86_64 machine, release build: 2.3 MB of prose
# from a 0.8 MB stream took 50 ms where liblzma through Python took 18,
# and 64 MiB of word-salad text 1.15 s where it took 0.47.
#
# Left out: compression, the BCJ filters but x86, reading a multi-block
# file's blocks in parallel (one from `xz -T` is read one block after
# another), and random access through the index.
#
# Strings are the byte type here, as everywhere in `src/std`: a
# compressed stream is a `String` whose bytes are the stream.

module std/xz

import std/int
import std/digest::{CRC32, CRC64, SHA256}
import std/static_array::{StaticArray}

# What `XzReader#read` and `Xz.decompress` answer for a stream they cannot
# read: one that is corrupt, whose check or index or sizes do not match,
# that ends early, or whose dictionary is past the caller's limit.
@[OnTape]
pub struct XzError
  getter message : String

  def initialize(@message : String)
  end

  def to_s : String
    @message
  end
end

impl Error for XzError
  def message : String
    @message
  end
end

# The two files LZMA travels in: the .xz container, and the .lzma file
# of LZMA Utils and the LZMA SDK.
pub enum XzFormat
  Xz
  Lzma
end

# The decoder: the containers' state machine around one LZMA decoder, the
# compressed bytes pulled into a buffer as they are needed and the
# decompressed ones written into the dictionary they are read from.
#
# The input is a buffer of IN_CAP bytes with SLACK zero bytes after what
# it holds. A piece the source gives is copied into it as room allows,
# so one piece the size of a whole file is taken 128 KiB at a time. The
# range coder reads it directly: before each symbol there are 21 bytes in
# hand, the most a symbol takes, or else everything there is (the rest
# of an LZMA2 chunk, or of the input once the source is done), and the
# zeros after it stand in for what a corrupt stream would read past its
# end, which the check after the symbol then refuses.
#
# The output is the dictionary, a ring: a match copies from behind the
# write position, `read` takes the oldest bytes not yet read, and what
# waits to be read is held under the ring's size, so a byte is never
# written over before it is read. The ring starts at 64 KiB, or the
# dictionary if that is smaller, and doubles each time the output fills
# it until it is the dictionary's size; only then does it wrap.
#
# A filter before LZMA2 (delta, x86) runs on the bytes as `read` takes
# them out of the ring, through a staging buffer where the x86 filter
# keeps the up to four bytes it cannot decide until more arrive. The
# block's check and size are taken over what `read` hands out.
class XzCore
  IN_CAP = 131072
  SLACK  =     64
  # The most input one LZMA symbol takes: XZ Embedded's LZMA_IN_REQUIRED.
  SYMBOL_BYTES =    21
  DICT_MIN     =  4096
  FIRST_RING   = 65536

  # Where each probability table starts (XZ Embedded's `struct lzma_dec`):
  # is_match[12][16], is_rep[12], is_rep0..2[12], is_rep0_long[12][16],
  # dist_slot[4][64], dist_special[114], dist_align[16], then the two
  # length coders (choice, choice2, low[16][8], mid[16][8], high[256]),
  # then the literal coders, 0x300 each.
  IS_MATCH     =    0
  IS_REP       =  192
  IS_REP0      =  204
  IS_REP1      =  216
  IS_REP2      =  228
  IS_REP0_LONG =  240
  DIST_SLOT    =  432
  DIST_SPECIAL =  688
  DIST_ALIGN   =  802
  MATCH_LEN    =  818
  REP_LEN      = 1332
  LITERAL      = 1846

  STREAM_HEAD =  0
  BLOCK_HEAD  =  1
  CHUNK       =  2
  LZMA        =  3
  COPY        =  4
  BLOCK_END   =  5
  PADDING     =  6
  ALONE_HEAD  =  7
  ALONE       =  8
  ALONE_END   =  9
  DONE        = 10

  FILTER_DELTA = 3
  FILTER_X86   = 4

  @format : XzFormat
  @dict_limit : Int64
  # The stream the pieces come from; nil when *data* was all of it.
  @io : IyiIO?
  # The whole input when it came as *data*, and how far it is copied in;
  # once the stream refills @chunk, the piece is @chunk's bytes, read
  # through a local view so no field keeps a view of what is refilled.
  @piece : String
  @streamed : Bool
  @piece_pos : Int32
  @exhausted : Bool
  @buf : Array(UInt8)
  @in_pos : Int32
  @in_end : Int32
  # Where in the whole input `@buf[0]` is.
  @in_base : Int64
  @state : Int32
  @failed : Bool
  @error : XzError
  @chunk : String::Builder
  @message : String::Builder
  # Set when a step stops for input it would have to wait for while
  # there are bytes to hand out.
  @waiting : Bool
  @scratch : Array(UInt8)

  # The dictionary ring.
  @dict : Array(UInt8)
  @dcap : Int32
  @dsize : Int32
  @dpos : Int32
  @written : Int64
  @pending : Int32

  # The LZMA decoder.
  @probs : Array(UInt16)
  @probs_cap : Int32
  @lc : Int32
  @lp : Int32
  @pb : Int32
  @lstate : Int32
  @rep0 : UInt32
  @rep1 : UInt32
  @rep2 : UInt32
  @rep3 : UInt32
  @len : Int32
  @rem : Int32
  @range : UInt32
  @code : UInt32
  # Where the range coder's input ends (an LZMA2 chunk's compressed size)
  # and how many bytes the LZMA data has left to give (-1: unknown).
  @lz_stop : Int64
  @lz_left : Int64
  @marker_next : Bool

  # LZMA2.
  @need_dict_reset : Bool
  @need_props : Bool
  @copy_left : Int32

  # The stream and the block.
  @check_id : Int32
  @stream_flags : Int32
  @crc32 : UInt32
  @crc64 : UInt64
  @sha : SHA256
  @digest : Array(UInt8)
  @header_size : Int32
  @data_start : Int64
  @data_end : Int64
  @declared_comp : Int64
  @declared_uncomp : Int64
  @block_out : Int64
  # What the block's LZMA2 chunks say they decode to, so far.
  @block_lz : Int64
  @blocks : Int64
  @sum_unpadded : Int64
  @sum_uncomp : Int64
  @records : UInt64

  # The filters before LZMA2, in the order they are undone.
  @nfilters : Int32
  @fkind : Array(Int32)
  @fdist : Array(Int32)
  @fhist : Array(UInt8)
  @fhpos : Array(Int32)
  @fx86pos : Array(UInt32)
  @fx86mask : Array(UInt32)
  # Where each filter's bytes not yet filtered start in the stage.
  @fu : Array(Int32)
  @stage : Array(UInt8)
  @stage_cap : Int32
  @sbeg : Int32
  @slen : Int32
  @ready : Int32

  def initialize(@format : XzFormat, @dict_limit : Int64, @io : IyiIO?, data : String)
    @piece = data
    @streamed = false
    @piece_pos = 0
    @exhausted = false
    @buf = Array(UInt8).new(IN_CAP + SLACK, 0_u8)
    @in_pos = 0
    @in_end = 0
    @in_base = 0_i64
    @state = @format == XzFormat::Xz ? STREAM_HEAD : ALONE_HEAD
    @failed = false
    @error = XzError.new("")
    @chunk = String::Builder.new(1)
    @message = String::Builder.new(128)
    @waiting = false
    @scratch = Array(UInt8).new(64, 0_u8)
    @dict = Array(UInt8).new
    @dcap = 0
    @dsize = DICT_MIN
    @dpos = 0
    @written = 0_i64
    @pending = 0
    @probs = Array(UInt16).new
    @probs_cap = 0
    @lc = 0
    @lp = 0
    @pb = 0
    @lstate = 0
    @rep0 = 0_u32
    @rep1 = 0_u32
    @rep2 = 0_u32
    @rep3 = 0_u32
    @len = 0
    @rem = 0
    @range = 0xffffffff_u32
    @code = 0_u32
    @lz_stop = 0_i64
    @lz_left = 0_i64
    @marker_next = false
    @need_dict_reset = true
    @need_props = true
    @copy_left = 0
    @check_id = 0
    @stream_flags = 0
    @crc32 = 0_u32
    @crc64 = 0_u64
    @sha = SHA256.new
    @digest = Array(UInt8).new(32, 0_u8)
    @header_size = 0
    @data_start = 0_i64
    @data_end = 0_i64
    @declared_comp = -1_i64
    @declared_uncomp = -1_i64
    @block_out = 0_i64
    @block_lz = 0_i64
    @blocks = 0_i64
    @sum_unpadded = 0_i64
    @sum_uncomp = 0_i64
    @records = 0_u64
    @nfilters = 0
    @fkind = Array(Int32).new(4, 0)
    @fdist = Array(Int32).new(4, 0)
    @fhist = Array(UInt8).new(1024, 0_u8)
    @fhpos = Array(Int32).new(4, 0)
    @fx86pos = Array(UInt32).new(4, 0_u32)
    @fx86mask = Array(UInt32).new(4, 0_u32)
    @fu = Array(Int32).new(4, 0)
    @stage = Array(UInt8).new
    @stage_cap = 0
    @sbeg = 0
    @slen = 0
    @ready = 0
  end

  def failed? : Bool
    @failed
  end

  def error : XzError
    @error
  end

  def finished? : Bool
    @state == DONE && @pending == 0 && @slen == @sbeg && !@failed
  end

  # Up to *max* bytes, "" at the end; see `XzReader#read`. The bytes are
  # read into a flat String, which moves down (SPEC 1.5); the answer only
  # wraps it.
  def read(max : Int32) : String | XzError
    answer(read_text(max))
  end

  private def answer(text : String) : String | XzError
    return @error if text.empty? && @failed
    text
  end

  private def read_text(max : Int32) : String
    raise "XzReader: read wants at least one byte, not #{max}" if max < 1
    return "" if @failed
    want = max < @dsize ? max : @dsize
    # The steps pick what to answer; the answer is made last.
    step = read_step(want)
    return "" if step == FAILED || step == ENDED
    n = step == READY ? @ready - @sbeg : @pending
    n = max if n > max
    String.build(n) do |dst|
      step == READY ? take_ready(dst, max) : take(dst, max)
    end
  end

  READY = 0
  FAILED = 1
  TAKE = 2
  ENDED = 3

  private def read_step(want : Int32) : Int32
    while true
      return READY if @ready > @sbeg
      run(want) if @pending < want
      return FAILED if @failed
      return TAKE if @nfilters == 0 && @slen == @sbeg
      pump(@state == BLOCK_END)
      return READY if @ready > @sbeg
      return ENDED if @state == DONE && @pending == 0
    end
    ENDED
  end

  # Every byte there is, into *sink*: `Xz.decompress`, without a string
  # for each piece.
  def drain(sink : String::Builder) : Nil
    while !@failed
      if @ready > @sbeg
        n = @ready - @sbeg
        account(@stage, @sbeg, n)
        XzCore.emit(sink, @stage, @sbeg, n)
        @sbeg = @ready
        next
      end
      run(@dsize) if @pending < @dsize
      return if @failed
      if @nfilters == 0 && @slen == @sbeg
        return if @pending == 0
        start = @dpos - @pending
        start = start + @dcap if start < 0
        first = @pending < @dcap - start ? @pending : @dcap - start
        account(@dict, start, first)
        XzCore.emit(sink, @dict, start, first)
        rest = @pending - first
        if rest > 0
          account(@dict, 0, rest)
          XzCore.emit(sink, @dict, 0, rest)
        end
        @pending = 0
        next
      end
      pump(@state == BLOCK_END)
      return if @ready == @sbeg && @state == DONE && @pending == 0
    end
  end

  # The oldest *max* bytes of the ring not yet read.
  private def take(dst : String::Builder, max : Int32) : Nil
    n = @pending < max ? @pending : max
    return if n == 0
    start = @dpos - @pending
    start = start + @dcap if start < 0
    first = n < @dcap - start ? n : @dcap - start
    @pending = @pending - n
    account(@dict, start, first)
    account(@dict, 0, n - first) if n > first
    XzCore.emit(dst, @dict, start, first)
    XzCore.emit(dst, @dict, 0, n - first) if n > first
  end

  # *n* bytes of *src* from *at* onto *sink*.
  def self.emit(sink : String::Builder, src : Array(UInt8), at : Int32, n : Int32) : Nil
    i = 0
    while i < n
      sink.push(src[at + i])
      i = i + 1
    end
  end

  # Up to *max* of the filtered bytes waiting in the stage.
  private def take_ready(dst : String::Builder, max : Int32) : Nil
    n = @ready - @sbeg
    n = max if n > max
    at = @sbeg
    @sbeg = @sbeg + n
    account(@stage, at, n)
    XzCore.emit(dst, @stage, at, n)
  end

  # The block's check and size over bytes handed out.
  private def account(src : Array(UInt8), at : Int32, n : Int32) : Nil
    return if n == 0
    @block_out = @block_out + n.to_i64
    case @check_id
    when  1 then @crc32 = CRC32.update(@crc32, src[at, n], n)
    when  4 then @crc64 = CRC64.update(@crc64, src[at, n], n)
    when 10 then @sha.update(src[at, n], n)
    end
    nil
  end

  # What waits in the ring into the stage, after what the filters held
  # back, and through the filters in the order they are undone: each
  # filters what the one before it let through, and keeps back what it
  # cannot decide yet. *final* is the block's end, where nothing more is
  # coming and what a filter kept back goes out as it is.
  private def pump(final : Bool) : Nil
    if @sbeg > 0
      live = @slen - @sbeg
      i = 0
      while i < live
        @stage[i] = @stage[@sbeg + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      k = 0
      while k < @nfilters
        @fu[k] = @fu[k] - @sbeg
        k = k + 1
      end
      @ready = @ready - @sbeg
      @slen = live
      @sbeg = 0
    end
    if @slen + @pending > @stage_cap
      cap = @slen + @pending + 64
      while @stage.size < cap
        @stage << 0_u8
      end
      @stage_cap = cap
    end
    if @pending > 0
      start = @dpos - @pending
      start = start + @dcap if start < 0
      first = @pending < @dcap - start ? @pending : @dcap - start
      i = 0
      while i < first
        @stage[@slen + i] = @dict[start + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      i = 0
      while i < @pending - first
        @stage[@slen + first + i] = @dict[i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      @slen = @slen + @pending
      @pending = 0
    end
    limit = @slen
    k = 0
    while k < @nfilters
      start = @fu[k]
      done = filter(k, start, limit - start)
      done = limit - start if final
      @fu[k] = start + done
      limit = start + done
      k = k + 1
    end
    @ready = limit
  end

  # Filter *k* undone over *n* bytes at *p*, in place: how many of them
  # it has decided.
  private def filter(k : Int32, at : Int32, n : Int32) : Int32
    if @fkind[k] == FILTER_DELTA
      delta(k, at, n)
      n
    else
      x86(k, at, n)
    end
  end

  # liblzma's `delta_decode`: each byte plus the byte *distance* before
  # it, from a history of 256 that runs downward.
  private def delta(k : Int32, at : Int32, n : Int32) : Nil
    hist = k * 256
    distance = @fdist[k]
    pos = @fhpos[k]
    i = 0
    while i < n
      b = @stage[at + i] &+ @fhist[hist + ((distance + pos) & 255)]
      @stage[at + i] = b
      @fhist[hist + (pos & 255)] = b
      pos = (pos - 1) & 255
      i = i + 1
    end
    @fhpos[k] = pos
  end

  # XZ Embedded's `bcj_x86`: a CALL (E8) or JMP (E9) whose 32-bit operand
  # looks like an address near the code (its top byte 00 or FF) had that
  # address made absolute by the encoder, which compresses better; it is
  # made relative again here. Whether a byte that looks like E8 is one
  # depends on the three before it (`prev_mask`), and the last four
  # bytes cannot be decided until what follows them arrives.
  private def x86(k : Int32, at : Int32, n : Int32) : Int32
    return 0 if n <= 4
    size = n - 4
    prev_pos = -1
    prev_mask = @fx86mask[k]
    pos = @fx86pos[k]
    i = 0
    while i < size
      if (@stage[at + i] & 0xfe_u8) != 0xe8_u8
        i = i + 1
        next
      end
      gap = i - prev_pos
      if gap > 3
        prev_mask = 0_u32
      else
        prev_mask = (prev_mask.unsafe_shl(gap - 1)) & 7_u32
        if prev_mask != 0_u32
          b = @stage[at + i + 4 - X86_BIT_NUM[prev_mask.to_i32]]
          if !X86_ALLOWED[prev_mask.to_i32] || b == 0_u8 || b == 0xff_u8
            prev_pos = i
            prev_mask = prev_mask.unsafe_shl(1) | 1_u32
            i = i + 1
            next
          end
        end
      end
      prev_pos = i
      top = @stage[at + i + 4]
      if top == 0_u8 || top == 0xff_u8
        src = @stage[at + i + 1].to_u32 | @stage[at + i + 2].to_u32.unsafe_shl(8) | @stage[at + i + 3].to_u32.unsafe_shl(16) | top.to_u32.unsafe_shl(24)
        dest = 0_u32
        while true
          dest = src &- (pos &+ i.to_u32 &+ 5_u32)
          break if prev_mask == 0_u32
          j = X86_BIT_NUM[prev_mask.to_i32] * 8
          b = dest.unsafe_shr(24 - j) & 255_u32
          break unless b == 0_u32 || b == 255_u32
          src = dest ^ (1_u32.unsafe_shl(32 - j) &- 1_u32)
        end
        dest = dest & 0x01ffffff_u32
        dest = dest | (0_u32 &- (dest & 0x01000000_u32))
        @stage[at + i + 1] = (dest & 255_u32).to_u8
        @stage[at + i + 2] = (dest.unsafe_shr(8) & 255_u32).to_u8
        @stage[at + i + 3] = (dest.unsafe_shr(16) & 255_u32).to_u8
        @stage[at + i + 4] = dest.unsafe_shr(24).to_u8
        i = i + 5
      else
        prev_mask = prev_mask.unsafe_shl(1) | 1_u32
        i = i + 1
      end
    end
    gap = i - prev_pos
    @fx86mask[k] = gap > 3 ? 0_u32 : prev_mask.unsafe_shl(gap - 1)
    @fx86pos[k] = pos &+ i.to_u32
    i
  end

  X86_ALLOWED = StaticArray[true, true, true, false, true, false, false, false]
  X86_BIT_NUM = StaticArray[0, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 3]

  # Steps until *want* bytes wait in the ring, the stream has ended, or
  # it has failed; or there are bytes to hand out and going on would call
  # the source, which might be a socket that holds back the next piece.
  def run(want : Int32) : Nil
    while !@failed && @state != DONE
      break if @pending >= want
      case @state
      when STREAM_HEAD then stream_head
      when BLOCK_HEAD  then block_head
      when CHUNK       then chunk
      when LZMA, ALONE then lzma(want)
      when COPY        then copy(want)
      when BLOCK_END
        break if @pending > 0 || @slen > @sbeg
        block_end
      when PADDING    then padding
      when ALONE_HEAD then alone_head
      else
        break if @pending > 0
        alone_end
      end
      if @waiting
        @waiting = false
        break
      end
    end
  end

  private def fail(message : String) : Nil
    return if @failed
    @failed = true
    # The message is the reader's, in its own builder, not the caller's
    # scratch. A reader fails once: the builder is never cleared.
    @message.append(message)
    @error = XzError.new(@message.finish)
    nil
  end

  # More of the source's bytes after the ones in hand, or false when it
  # has none.
  private def fill : Bool
    if @piece_pos >= piece_size
      return false if @exhausted
      io = @io
      # The chunk is refilled in place: its bytes were all copied out.
      @piece = ""
      @streamed = true
      @chunk.clear
      got = io ? io.read_str(65536, @chunk) : 0
      if got == 0
        @exhausted = true
        return false
      end
      @piece_pos = 0
    end
    piece = @streamed ? @chunk.finish : @piece
    if @in_pos > 0
      rest = @in_end - @in_pos
      i = 0
      while i < rest
        @buf[i] = @buf[@in_pos + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      @in_base = @in_base + @in_pos.to_i64
      @in_end = rest
      @in_pos = 0
    end
    n = piece.bytesize - @piece_pos
    n = IN_CAP - @in_end if n > IN_CAP - @in_end
    i = 0
    while i < n
      @buf[@in_end + i] = piece.byte_at(@piece_pos + i)
      i = i + 1
    end
    @piece_pos = @piece_pos + n
    @in_end = @in_end + n
    i = 0
    while i < SLACK
      @buf[@in_end + i] = 0_u8
      i = i + 1
    end
    true
  end

  # Whether getting more input would mean calling the source.
  private def dry? : Bool
    @piece_pos >= piece_size && !@exhausted
  end

  # How many bytes the piece being copied in has.
  private def piece_size : Int32
    @streamed ? @chunk.bytesize : @piece.bytesize
  end

  # Whether *n* bytes are in hand, after taking what the source has.
  private def ahead?(n : Int32) : Bool
    while @in_end - @in_pos < n
      return false unless fill
    end
    true
  end

  # The next byte, or -1 at the end of the input.
  private def byte : Int32
    if @in_pos >= @in_end
      return -1 unless fill
    end
    b = @buf[@in_pos]
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 1
    b.to_i32
  end

  private def at : Int64
    @in_base + @in_pos.to_i64
  end

  # The little-endian words at @buf[*p*].
  private def le32(p : Int32) : UInt32
    @buf[p].to_u32 | @buf[p + 1].to_u32.unsafe_shl(8) | @buf[p + 2].to_u32.unsafe_shl(16) | @buf[p + 3].to_u32.unsafe_shl(24)
  end

  private def le64(p : Int32) : UInt64
    le32(p).to_u64 | le32(p + 4).to_u64.unsafe_shl(32)
  end

  # A size as people say it: "64 MiB", "12 KiB", "1000 bytes".
  def self.size_name(n : Int64) : String
    return "#{n.unsafe_shr(20)} MiB" if n >= 1048576_i64 && (n & 1048575_i64) == 0_i64
    return "#{n.unsafe_shr(10)} KiB" if n >= 1024_i64 && (n & 1023_i64) == 0_i64
    "#{n} bytes"
  end

  def self.hex(v : UInt64, digits : Int32) : String
    chars = "0123456789abcdef"
    String.build(digits) do |dst|
      i = 0
      while i < digits
        dst.push(chars.byte_at((v.unsafe_shr((digits - 1 - i) * 4) & 15_u64).to_i32))
        i = i + 1
      end
    end
  end

  # ---- the dictionary ----

  # A dictionary of *size* bytes for the block or stream that starts: the
  # ring keeps its memory, and grows toward *size* as it fills.
  private def dict_setup(size : Int64) : Nil
    @dsize = size < DICT_MIN.to_i64 ? DICT_MIN : size.to_i32
    if @dcap == 0
      @dcap = @dsize < FIRST_RING ? @dsize : FIRST_RING
      while @dict.size < @dcap
        @dict << 0_u8
      end
      @dpos = 0
    end
    @written = 0_i64
  end

  # The write position at the end of the ring: grow it if it is smaller
  # than the dictionary, else wrap.
  private def wrap : Nil
    if @dcap < @dsize
      cap = @dcap.to_i64 * 2_i64
      cap = @dsize.to_i64 if cap > @dsize.to_i64
      while @dict.size < cap
        @dict << 0_u8
      end
      @dcap = cap.to_i32
    else
      @dpos = 0
    end
  end

  private def put(b : UInt8) : Nil
    wrap if @dpos == @dcap
    @dict[@dpos] = b
    @dpos = @dpos + 1
    @written = @written + 1_i64
    @pending = @pending + 1
  end

  # *n* bytes from *src* (the input), as an uncompressed chunk has them.
  private def put_bytes(src : Int32, n : Int32) : Nil
    done = 0
    while done < n
      wrap if @dpos == @dcap
      k = n - done
      k = @dcap - @dpos if k > @dcap - @dpos
      i = 0
      while i < k
        @dict[@dpos + i] = @buf[src + done + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      @dpos = @dpos + k
      done = done + k
    end
    @written = @written + n.to_i64
    @pending = @pending + n
  end

  # The byte *distance* + 1 back from the write position.
  private def back(distance : Int32) : Int32
    i = @dpos - distance - 1
    i = i + @dcap if i < 0
    @dict[i].to_i32
  end

  # *n* bytes from *distance* back, which may overlap what they write;
  # eight at a time where the source is eight or more behind or wrapped
  # ahead, so no word reads what the same copy has not written yet.
  private def copy_match(distance : Int32, n : Int32) : Nil
    left = n
    while left > 0
      wrap if @dpos == @dcap
      src = @dpos - distance
      src = src + @dcap if src < 0
      k = left
      k = @dcap - @dpos if k > @dcap - @dpos
      k = @dcap - src if k > @dcap - src
      i = 0
      while i < k
        @dict[@dpos + i] = @dict[src + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
      @dpos = @dpos + k
      left = left - k
    end
    @written = @written + n.to_i64
    @pending = @pending + n
  end

  # ---- the range coder and the LZMA decoder ----

  # The range coder's start: five bytes, the first always zero (liblzma
  # refuses one that is not), the other four the code.
  private def rc_init(who : String) : Bool
    unless ahead?(5)
      fail("#{who}: the stream ends inside the range coder's first bytes")
      return false
    end
    unless @buf[@in_pos] == 0_u8
      fail("#{who}: the range coder's first byte is not zero")
      return false
    end
    @code = @buf[@in_pos + 1].to_u32.unsafe_shl(24) | @buf[@in_pos + 2].to_u32.unsafe_shl(16) |
            @buf[@in_pos + 3].to_u32.unsafe_shl(8) | @buf[@in_pos + 4].to_u32
    @range = 0xffffffff_u32
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 5
    true
  end

  private def normalize : Nil
    if @range < 0x1000000_u32
      @range = @range.unsafe_shl(8)
      @code = @code.unsafe_shl(8) | @buf[@in_pos].to_u32
      @in_pos = @in_pos + 1
    end
  end

  # One bit by the probability at *i*, which learns from it.
  private def bit(i : Int32) : Int32
    normalize
    prob = @probs[i].to_u32
    bound = @range.unsafe_shr(11) &* prob
    if @code < bound
      @range = bound
      @probs[i] = (prob + (2048_u32 - prob).unsafe_shr(5)).unsafe_to_u16
      0
    else
      @range = @range - bound
      @code = @code - bound
      @probs[i] = (prob - prob.unsafe_shr(5)).unsafe_to_u16
      1
    end
  end

  # A symbol of a bit tree whose leaves start at *limit*, most significant
  # bit first; the answer is the leaf, *limit* to 2 * *limit* - 1.
  private def tree(base : Int32, limit : Int32) : Int32
    symbol = 1
    while symbol < limit
      symbol = (symbol << 1) + bit(base + symbol)
    end
    symbol
  end

  # *bits* bits of a bit tree, least significant first.
  private def reverse(base : Int32, bits : Int32) : UInt32
    symbol = 1
    result = 0_u32
    i = 0
    while i < bits
      b = bit(base + symbol)
      symbol = (symbol << 1) + b
      result = result | b.to_u32.unsafe_shl(i)
      i = i + 1
    end
    result
  end

  # *bits* bits at even odds, most significant first.
  private def direct(bits : Int32) : UInt32
    result = 0_u32
    i = 0
    while i < bits
      normalize
      @range = @range.unsafe_shr(1)
      if @code >= @range
        @code = @code - @range
        result = result.unsafe_shl(1) | 1_u32
      else
        result = result.unsafe_shl(1)
      end
      i = i + 1
    end
    result
  end

  # lc, lp and pb from the properties byte (pb * 5 + lp) * 9 + lc.
  private def lzma_props(props : Int32) : Nil
    @lc = props % 9
    @lp = (props // 9) % 5
    @pb = props // 45
    count = LITERAL + (0x300 << (@lc + @lp))
    if count > @probs_cap
      while @probs.size < count
        @probs << 0_u16
      end
      @probs_cap = count
    end
  end

  # The state reset: every probability at one half, the state and the
  # repeated distances to their start.
  private def lzma_reset : Nil
    count = LITERAL + (0x300 << (@lc + @lp))
    i = 0
    while i < count
      @probs[i] = 1024_u16
      i = i + 1
    end
    @lstate = 0
    @rep0 = 0_u32
    @rep1 = 0_u32
    @rep2 = 0_u32
    @rep3 = 0_u32
    @rem = 0
  end

  private def match_len(base : Int32, pos_state : Int32) : Int32
    if bit(base) == 0
      2 + tree(base + 2 + pos_state * 8, 8) - 8
    elsif bit(base + 1) == 0
      10 + tree(base + 130 + pos_state * 8, 8) - 8
    else
      18 + tree(base + 258, 256) - 256
    end
  end

  # The bytes the LZMA data decodes to, until *want* wait in the ring or
  # the data's uncompressed size is reached.
  private def lzma(want : Int32) : Nil
    who = @state == LZMA ? "LZMA2" : "lzma"
    pos_mask = (1 << @pb) - 1
    lit_mask = (1 << @lp) - 1
    while @pending < want
      if @rem > 0
        n = want - @pending
        n = @rem if n > @rem
        copy_match(@rep0.to_i32 + 1, n)
        @rem = @rem - n
        @lz_left = @lz_left - n.to_i64 if @lz_left > 0_i64
        next
      end
      # The input for the next symbol: 21 bytes, or the rest of the
      # chunk, or the rest of everything.
      if @in_end - @in_pos < SYMBOL_BYTES
        left = @lz_stop - at
        need = left < SYMBOL_BYTES.to_i64 ? left.to_i32 : SYMBOL_BYTES
        while @in_end - @in_pos < need
          if @pending > 0 && dry?
            @waiting = true
            return
          end
          break unless fill
        end
      end
      if @lz_left == 0_i64 && !@marker_next
        lzma_end(who)
        return
      end
      pos_state = (@written & pos_mask.to_i64).to_i32
      st = @lstate
      if bit(IS_MATCH + (st << 4) + pos_state) == 0
        return corrupt(who, "lzma: the data goes on past the uncompressed size its header gives") if @lz_left == 0_i64
        prev = @written > 0_i64 ? back(0) : 0
        base = LITERAL + 0x300 * ((((@written & lit_mask.to_i64).to_i32) << @lc) + (prev >> (8 - @lc)))
        symbol = 1
        if st < 7
          symbol = tree(base, 0x100)
        else
          match_byte = back(@rep0.to_i32) << 1
          offset = 0x100
          while symbol < 0x100
            match_bit = match_byte & offset
            match_byte = match_byte << 1
            if bit(base + offset + match_bit + symbol) == 1
              symbol = (symbol << 1) + 1
              offset = match_bit
            else
              symbol = symbol << 1
              offset = offset ^ match_bit
            end
          end
        end
        put((symbol & 0xff).to_u8)
        @lstate = st <= 3 ? 0 : (st <= 9 ? st - 3 : st - 6)
        @lz_left = @lz_left - 1_i64 if @lz_left > 0_i64
      else
        if bit(IS_REP + st) == 1
          return corrupt(who, "#{who}: a repeated match before any byte") if @written == 0_i64
          rep_match(st, pos_state)
        else
          new_match(st, pos_state)
          if @rep0 == 0xffffffff_u32
            end_marker(who)
            return
          end
        end
        return corrupt(who, "#{who}: a distance reaches before the output began") if @rep0.to_i64 >= @written
        return corrupt(who, "#{who}: a distance reaches past the dictionary") if @rep0.to_i64 >= @dsize.to_i64
        if @lz_left >= 0_i64 && @len.to_i64 > @lz_left
          return corrupt(who, @state == LZMA ? "LZMA2: a match runs past the end of its chunk" : "lzma: the data goes on past the uncompressed size its header gives")
        end
        @rem = @len
      end
      return if overrun(who)
    end
  end

  # What a symbol found wrong, unless it read past the input it had, which
  # is what went wrong first: the zeros after the input are not a stream.
  private def corrupt(who : String, message : String) : Nil
    fail(message) unless overrun(who)
  end

  # Whether the last symbol read past the input it had: past the end of
  # everything, or past its chunk.
  private def overrun(who : String) : Bool
    if @in_pos > @in_end
      fail(@state == LZMA ? "xz: the stream ends inside a block" : "lzma: the stream ends inside the LZMA data")
      return true
    end
    if at > @lz_stop
      fail("LZMA2: a chunk's data runs past its compressed size")
      return true
    end
    false
  end

  private def rep_match(st : Int32, pos_state : Int32) : Nil
    if bit(IS_REP0 + st) == 0
      if bit(IS_REP0_LONG + (st << 4) + pos_state) == 0
        @lstate = st < 7 ? 9 : 11
        @len = 1
        return
      end
    else
      tmp = 0_u32
      if bit(IS_REP1 + st) == 0
        tmp = @rep1
      else
        if bit(IS_REP2 + st) == 0
          tmp = @rep2
        else
          tmp = @rep3
          @rep3 = @rep2
        end
        @rep2 = @rep1
      end
      @rep1 = @rep0
      @rep0 = tmp
    end
    @lstate = st < 7 ? 8 : 11
    @len = match_len(REP_LEN, pos_state)
  end

  private def new_match(st : Int32, pos_state : Int32) : Nil
    @lstate = st < 7 ? 7 : 10
    @rep3 = @rep2
    @rep2 = @rep1
    @rep1 = @rep0
    @len = match_len(MATCH_LEN, pos_state)
    dist_state = @len < 6 ? @len - 2 : 3
    slot = tree(DIST_SLOT + dist_state * 64, 64) - 64
    if slot < 4
      @rep0 = slot.to_u32
      return
    end
    limit = (slot >> 1) - 1
    r = (2 | (slot & 1)).to_u32
    if slot < 14
      r = r.unsafe_shl(limit)
      r = r + reverse(DIST_SPECIAL + r.to_i32 - slot - 1, limit)
    else
      r = r.unsafe_shl(limit - 4) | direct(limit - 4)
      r = r.unsafe_shl(4) | reverse(DIST_ALIGN, 4)
    end
    @rep0 = r
  end

  # The LZMA data's uncompressed size reached: an LZMA2 chunk must end
  # there, its range coder at zero; a .lzma stream may, or may go on to
  # an end marker.
  private def lzma_end(who : String) : Nil
    normalize
    return if overrun(who)
    if @state == LZMA
      return fail("LZMA2: a chunk's data ends before its compressed size") unless at == @lz_stop
      return fail("LZMA2: the range coder does not end at zero") unless @code == 0_u32
      @state = CHUNK
    elsif @code == 0_u32
      @state = ALONE_END
    else
      @marker_next = true
    end
  end

  private def end_marker(who : String) : Nil
    return fail("LZMA2: an end marker inside a chunk") if @state == LZMA
    normalize
    return if overrun(who)
    return fail("lzma: the range coder does not end at zero after the end marker") unless @code == 0_u32
    return fail("lzma: the end marker comes before the uncompressed size its header gives") if @lz_left > 0_i64
    @state = ALONE_END
  end

  # ---- the .xz container ----

  # The stream header (§2.1.1): the magic, the flags - the check type -
  # and their CRC32.
  private def stream_head : Nil
    return fail("xz: the stream is shorter than its header") unless ahead?(12)
    h = @in_pos
    unless @buf[h + 0] == 0xfd_u8 && @buf[h + 1] == 0x37_u8 && @buf[h + 2] == 0x7a_u8 && @buf[h + 3] == 0x58_u8 && @buf[h + 4] == 0x5a_u8 && @buf[h + 5] == 0_u8
      return fail("xz: not an xz stream (the magic bytes are not FD 37 7A 58 5A 00)")
    end
    return fail("xz: the stream header's CRC32 does not match") unless CRC32.update(0_u32, @buf[h + 6, 2], 2) == le32(h + 8)
    return fail("xz: the stream flags have reserved bits set") unless @buf[h + 6] == 0_u8 && (@buf[h + 7] & 0xf0_u8) == 0_u8
    id = @buf[h + 7].to_i32
    unless id == 0 || id == 1 || id == 4 || id == 10
      return fail("xz: check type #{id} is not one this reader verifies (none, CRC32, CRC64 or SHA-256)")
    end
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 12
    @check_id = id
    @stream_flags = id
    @blocks = 0_i64
    @sum_unpadded = 0_i64
    @sum_uncomp = 0_i64
    @records = 0_u64
    @state = BLOCK_HEAD
  end

  # A variable-length integer of the format (§1.2) at *p*[*i*], below
  # *stop*: seven bits a byte, the least significant first, nine bytes at
  # most and no zero byte at the end of a longer one. -1 for one that is
  # not; `@vat` is where it ended.
  @vat = 0

  private def vli(p : Int32, i : Int32, stop : Int32) : Int64
    v = 0_i64
    k = 0
    j = i
    while true
      return -1_i64 if j >= stop || k >= 9
      b = @buf[p + j]
      j = j + 1
      v = v | (b & 0x7f_u8).to_i64.unsafe_shl(k * 7)
      if (b & 0x80_u8) == 0_u8
        return -1_i64 if b == 0_u8 && k > 0
        break
      end
      k = k + 1
    end
    @vat = j
    v
  end

  # A block header (§3.1), or the index where a block would start.
  private def block_head : Nil
    return fail("xz: the stream ends before its index") unless ahead?(1)
    first = @buf[@in_pos].to_i32
    if first == 0
      index
      return
    end
    size = (first + 1) * 4
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block header") unless ahead?(size)
    h = @in_pos
    return fail("xz: a block header's CRC32 does not match") unless CRC32.update(0_u32, @buf[h, size - 4], size - 4) == le32(h + size - 4)
    flags = @buf[h + 1].to_i32
    return fail("xz: a block header has reserved flags set") unless (flags & 0x3c) == 0
    stop = size - 4
    i = 2
    @declared_comp = -1_i64
    @declared_uncomp = -1_i64
    if (flags & 0x40) != 0
      @declared_comp = vli(h, i, stop)
      return fail("xz: a block header's compressed size is not a number") if @declared_comp < 0_i64
      return fail("xz: a block header gives a compressed size of zero") if @declared_comp == 0_i64
      # The block's unpadded size - header, data, check - must stay under
      # 2^63 (§3.1.3), so a size past that is refused here, before any of
      # the data it would describe is decoded.
      if @declared_comp > 0x7ffffffffffffffc_i64 - size.to_i64 - XzCore.check_size(@check_id).to_i64
        return fail("xz: a block header's compressed size is past what a block can hold")
      end
      i = @vat
    end
    if (flags & 0x80) != 0
      @declared_uncomp = vli(h, i, stop)
      return fail("xz: a block header's uncompressed size is not a number") if @declared_uncomp < 0_i64
      i = @vat
    end
    count = (flags & 3) + 1
    dict = 0_i64
    @nfilters = 0
    k = 0
    while k < count
      id = vli(h, i, stop)
      return fail("xz: a block header's filter is not a number") if id < 0_i64
      i = @vat
      psize = vli(h, i, stop)
      return fail("xz: a block header's filter properties are not a number") if psize < 0_i64
      i = @vat
      return fail("xz: a filter's properties run past its block header") if psize > (stop - i).to_i64
      props = h + i
      plen = psize.to_i32
      i = i + plen
      last = k == count - 1
      if id == 0x21_i64
        return fail("xz: LZMA2 is not the last filter") unless last
        return fail("xz: LZMA2's properties are not one byte") unless plen == 1
        d = @buf[props].to_i32
        return fail("xz: LZMA2's dictionary property has reserved bits set") unless (d & 0xc0) == 0
        return fail("xz: LZMA2's dictionary property is past 40") if d > 40
        dict = d == 40 ? 0xffffffff_i64 : (2_i64 | (d & 1).to_i64).unsafe_shl(d // 2 + 11)
      elsif last
        return fail("xz: the last filter is not LZMA2")
      elsif id == 0x03_i64
        return fail("xz: the delta filter's properties are not one byte") unless plen == 1
        slot = count - 2 - k
        @fkind[slot] = FILTER_DELTA
        @fdist[slot] = @buf[props].to_i32 + 1
        @fhpos[slot] = 0
        z = 0
        while z < 256
          @fhist[slot * 256 + z] = 0_u8
          z = z + 1
        end
        @nfilters = @nfilters + 1
      elsif id == 0x04_i64
        return fail("xz: the x86 filter's properties are not zero or four bytes") unless plen == 0 || plen == 4
        slot = count - 2 - k
        @fkind[slot] = FILTER_X86
        @fx86pos[slot] = plen == 4 ? le32(props) : 0_u32
        @fx86mask[slot] = 0_u32
        @nfilters = @nfilters + 1
      else
        return fail("xz: filter #{XzCore.filter_name(id)} is not supported")
      end
      k = k + 1
    end
    while i < stop
      return fail("xz: a block header's padding is not zero") unless @buf[h + i] == 0_u8
      i = i + 1
    end
    if dict > @dict_limit
      return fail("xz: the block's dictionary is #{XzCore.size_name(dict)}, past the limit of #{XzCore.size_name(@dict_limit)}")
    end
    @in_pos = @in_pos + size
    @header_size = size
    @data_start = at
    dict_setup(dict)
    k = 0
    while k < @nfilters
      @fu[k] = 0
      k = k + 1
    end
    @sbeg = 0
    @slen = 0
    @ready = 0
    @crc32 = 0_u32
    @crc64 = 0_u64
    @sha.reset
    @block_out = 0_i64
    @block_lz = 0_i64
    @need_dict_reset = true
    @need_props = true
    @state = CHUNK
  end

  def self.filter_name(id : Int64) : String
    case id
    when 0x05_i64 then "0x05 (PowerPC BCJ)"
    when 0x06_i64 then "0x06 (IA-64 BCJ)"
    when 0x07_i64 then "0x07 (ARM BCJ)"
    when 0x08_i64 then "0x08 (ARM-Thumb BCJ)"
    when 0x09_i64 then "0x09 (SPARC BCJ)"
    when 0x0a_i64 then "0x0a (ARM64 BCJ)"
    when 0x0b_i64 then "0x0b (RISC-V BCJ)"
    else               "0x#{XzCore.hex(id.to_u64, 2)}"
    end
  end

  # An LZMA2 chunk's header (the control byte and the sizes and
  # properties it says follow), or the end of the LZMA2 data.
  private def chunk : Nil
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless ahead?(1)
    c = @buf[@in_pos].to_i32
    if c == 0
      @in_pos = @in_pos + 1
      @data_end = at
      @state = BLOCK_END
      return
    end
    if c >= 0xe0 || c == 1
      @need_props = true
      @need_dict_reset = false
      @written = 0_i64
    elsif @need_dict_reset
      return fail("LZMA2: the first chunk does not reset the dictionary")
    end
    if c >= 0x80
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless ahead?(c >= 0xc0 ? 6 : 5)
      h = @in_pos
      return unless within(c >= 0xc0 ? 6 : 5, (@buf[h + 3].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[h + 4].to_i32 + 1, ((c & 0x1f) << 16) + (@buf[h + 1].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[h + 2].to_i32 + 1)
    elsif c <= 2
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless ahead?(3)
      size = (@buf[@in_pos + 1].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[@in_pos + 2].to_i32 + 1
      return unless within(3, size, size)
    end
    if c >= 0x80
      head = c >= 0xc0 ? 6 : 5
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless ahead?(head)
      h = @in_pos
      unpacked = ((c & 0x1f) << 16) + (@buf[h + 1].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[h + 2].to_i32 + 1
      packed = (@buf[h + 3].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[h + 4].to_i32 + 1
      if c >= 0xc0
        props = @buf[h + 5].to_i32
        return fail("LZMA2: a properties byte past 224") if props > 224
        return fail("LZMA2: lc + lp is past 4") if props % 9 + (props // 9) % 5 > 4
        lzma_props(props)
        @need_props = false
        lzma_reset
      elsif @need_props
        return fail("LZMA2: a chunk without properties where they are needed")
      elsif c >= 0xa0
        lzma_reset
      end
      @in_pos = @in_pos + head
      return fail("LZMA2: a chunk shorter than its range coder's first bytes") if packed < 5
      @lz_stop = at + packed.to_i64
      return unless rc_init("LZMA2")
      @lz_left = unpacked.to_i64
      @marker_next = false
      @state = LZMA
    else
      return fail("LZMA2: control byte 0x#{XzCore.hex(c.to_u64, 2)} is not one LZMA2 defines") if c > 2
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless ahead?(3)
      @copy_left = (@buf[@in_pos + 1].to_i32 << 8) + @buf[@in_pos + 2].to_i32 + 1
      @in_pos = @in_pos + 3
      @state = COPY
    end
  end

  # Whether a chunk of *head* + *packed* bytes that decodes to *unpacked*
  # stays inside the sizes the block header gave, as liblzma holds a
  # block to them: a block that would go past either is refused before
  # the chunk is decoded, rather than after what it held was handed out.
  private def within(head : Int32, packed : Int32, unpacked : Int32) : Bool
    if @declared_comp >= 0_i64 && at + head.to_i64 + packed.to_i64 - @data_start >= @declared_comp
      fail("xz: a block's data runs past the compressed size its header gives")
      return false
    end
    @block_lz = @block_lz + unpacked.to_i64
    if @declared_uncomp >= 0_i64 && @block_lz > @declared_uncomp
      fail("xz: a block's data goes past the uncompressed size its header gives")
      return false
    end
    true
  end

  # An uncompressed chunk's bytes, into the dictionary as they are.
  private def copy(want : Int32) : Nil
    while @copy_left > 0
      return if @pending >= want
      if @in_pos >= @in_end
        if @pending > 0 && dry?
          @waiting = true
          return
        end
        return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block") unless fill
      end
      n = @copy_left
      n = @in_end - @in_pos if n > @in_end - @in_pos
      n = want - @pending if n > want - @pending
      put_bytes(@in_pos, n)
      @in_pos = @in_pos + n
      @copy_left = @copy_left - n
    end
    @state = CHUNK
  end

  # After the block's data, once every byte of it has been handed out:
  # its sizes against its header, its padding, its check.
  private def block_end : Nil
    comp = @data_end - @data_start
    if @declared_comp >= 0_i64 && @declared_comp != comp
      return fail("xz: a block's compressed size does not match its header (#{comp}, header says #{@declared_comp})")
    end
    if @declared_uncomp >= 0_i64 && @declared_uncomp != @block_out
      return fail("xz: a block's uncompressed size does not match its header (#{@block_out}, header says #{@declared_uncomp})")
    end
    pad = ((4_i64 - (comp & 3_i64)) & 3_i64).to_i32
    size = XzCore.check_size(@check_id)
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside a block's padding or check") unless ahead?(pad + size)
    i = 0
    while i < pad
      return fail("xz: a block's padding is not zero") unless @buf[@in_pos + i] == 0_u8
      i = i + 1
    end
    c = @in_pos + pad
    case @check_id
    when 1
      want = le32(c)
      return fail("xz: a block's CRC32 does not match (#{XzCore.hex(@crc32.to_u64, 8)}, stream says #{XzCore.hex(want.to_u64, 8)})") unless want == @crc32
    when 4
      want = le64(c)
      return fail("xz: a block's CRC64 does not match (#{XzCore.hex(@crc64, 16)}, stream says #{XzCore.hex(want, 16)})") unless want == @crc64
    when 10
      digest = @digest
      @sha.final(digest)
      i = 0
      while i < 32
        return fail("xz: a block's SHA-256 does not match") unless digest[i] == @buf[c + i]
        i = i + 1
      end
    end
    @in_pos = @in_pos + pad + size
    record(@header_size.to_i64 + comp + size.to_i64, @block_out)
    @state = BLOCK_HEAD
  end

  def self.check_size(id : Int32) : Int32
    case id
    when  1 then 4
    when  4 then 8
    when 10 then 32
    else         0
    end
  end

  # One block as the index will list it: counted, summed, and folded into
  # a CRC-64 of the records, which the index's records must reproduce.
  private def record(unpadded : Int64, uncomp : Int64) : Nil
    @blocks = @blocks + 1_i64
    @sum_unpadded = @sum_unpadded &+ unpadded
    @sum_uncomp = @sum_uncomp &+ uncomp
    p = @scratch
    i = 0
    while i < 8
      p[i] = (unpadded.unsafe_shr(i * 8) & 255_i64).to_u8
      p[8 + i] = (uncomp.unsafe_shr(i * 8) & 255_i64).to_u8
      i = i + 1
    end
    @records = CRC64.update(@records, p[0, 16], 16)
  end

  # A variable-length integer read from the stream, each byte into the
  # index's CRC32; -1 for one that is not, -2 for the stream ending.
  @icrc = 0_u32
  @isize = 0_i64

  private def index_byte : Int32
    b = byte
    if b >= 0
      @icrc = CRC32.update_byte(@icrc, b.to_u8)
      @isize = @isize + 1_i64
    end
    b
  end

  private def index_vli : Int64
    v = 0_i64
    k = 0
    while true
      return -1_i64 if k >= 9
      b = index_byte
      return -2_i64 if b < 0
      v = v | (b & 0x7f).to_i64.unsafe_shl(k * 7)
      if (b & 0x80) == 0
        return -1_i64 if b == 0 && k > 0
        break
      end
      k = k + 1
    end
    v
  end

  # The index (§4) and the stream footer (§2.1.2), checked against the
  # blocks the stream had.
  private def index : Nil
    @icrc = 0_u32
    @isize = 0_i64
    index_byte
    count = index_vli
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside its index") if count == -2_i64
    return fail("xz: the index's record count is not a number") if count < 0_i64
    return fail("xz: the index lists #{count} blocks where the stream has #{@blocks}") unless count == @blocks
    sum_unpadded = 0_i64
    sum_uncomp = 0_i64
    records = 0_u64
    n = 0_i64
    while n < count
      unpadded = index_vli
      uncomp = unpadded < 0_i64 ? unpadded : index_vli
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside its index") if unpadded == -2_i64 || uncomp == -2_i64
      return fail("xz: an index record is not a number") if unpadded < 0_i64 || uncomp < 0_i64
      # The smallest block is a header, a byte of data and no check, and
      # none reaches 2^63; nor do all of a stream's put together.
      if unpadded < 5_i64 || unpadded > 0x7ffffffffffffffc_i64
        return fail("xz: an index record's unpadded size is not one a block can have")
      end
      return fail("xz: the index's uncompressed sizes add up past 2^63") if uncomp > 0x7fffffffffffffff_i64 - sum_uncomp
      sum_unpadded = sum_unpadded &+ unpadded
      sum_uncomp = sum_uncomp &+ uncomp
      p = @scratch
      i = 0
      while i < 8
        p[i] = (unpadded.unsafe_shr(i * 8) & 255_i64).to_u8
        p[8 + i] = (uncomp.unsafe_shr(i * 8) & 255_i64).to_u8
        i = i + 1
      end
      records = CRC64.update(records, p[0, 16], 16)
      n = n + 1_i64
    end
    unless sum_unpadded == @sum_unpadded && sum_uncomp == @sum_uncomp && records == @records
      return fail("xz: the index does not match the blocks")
    end
    while (@isize & 3_i64) != 0_i64
      b = index_byte
      return fail("xz: the stream ends inside its index") if b < 0
      return fail("xz: the index's padding is not zero") unless b == 0
    end
    want = @icrc
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside its index") unless ahead?(4)
    return fail("xz: the index's CRC32 does not match") unless le32(@in_pos) == want
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 4
    index_size = @isize + 4_i64
    return fail("xz: the stream ends inside its footer") unless ahead?(12)
    f = @in_pos
    return fail("xz: the stream footer's CRC32 does not match") unless CRC32.update(0_u32, @buf[f + 4, 6], 6) == le32(f)
    return fail("xz: the stream footer's magic bytes are not YZ") unless @buf[f + 10] == 0x59_u8 && @buf[f + 11] == 0x5a_u8
    return fail("xz: the stream footer's flags do not match its header") unless @buf[f + 8] == 0_u8 && @buf[f + 9].to_i32 == @stream_flags
    backward = (le32(f + 4).to_i64 + 1_i64) * 4_i64
    return fail("xz: the stream footer's index size does not match the index") unless backward == index_size
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 12
    @state = PADDING
  end

  # Stream padding (§2.2): zero bytes, four at a time, then the end or
  # another stream.
  private def padding : Nil
    zeros = 0
    while true
      unless ahead?(1)
        return fail("xz: the stream padding is not a multiple of four bytes") unless (zeros & 3) == 0
        @state = DONE
        return
      end
      b = @buf[@in_pos]
      if b == 0_u8
        @in_pos = @in_pos + 1
        zeros = zeros + 1
        next
      end
      return fail("xz: the stream padding is not a multiple of four bytes") unless (zeros & 3) == 0
      return fail("xz: what follows the stream is neither padding nor another stream") unless b == 0xfd_u8
      @state = STREAM_HEAD
      return
    end
  end

  # ---- the .lzma file ----

  # The 13-byte header: the properties byte, the dictionary size, and the
  # uncompressed size, all ones for "unknown, ended by a marker".
  private def alone_head : Nil
    return fail("lzma: the stream is shorter than its 13-byte header") unless ahead?(13)
    h = @in_pos
    props = @buf[h + 0].to_i32
    return fail("lzma: the properties byte is past 224 (#{props})") if props > 224
    dict = le32(h + 1).to_i64
    size = le64(h + 5)
    if dict > @dict_limit
      return fail("lzma: the dictionary is #{XzCore.size_name(dict)}, past the limit of #{XzCore.size_name(@dict_limit)}")
    end
    return fail("lzma: the uncompressed size is past 2^63") if size != 0xffffffffffffffff_u64 && size >= 0x8000000000000000_u64
    @in_pos = @in_pos + 13
    lzma_props(props)
    lzma_reset
    dict_setup(dict)
    @lz_left = size == 0xffffffffffffffff_u64 ? -1_i64 : size.to_i64
    @lz_stop = 0x7fffffffffffffff_i64
    @marker_next = false
    @state = ALONE
    rc_init("lzma")
  end

  # The end of the .lzma data, once it has all been handed out: nothing
  # may follow.
  private def alone_end : Nil
    return fail("lzma: bytes follow the end of the stream") if ahead?(1)
    @state = DONE
  end
end

# A .xz or .lzma stream read a piece at a time: the compressed bytes come
# from the block, the decompressed ones go out through `read`, and memory
# stays at the stream's dictionary and what is waiting to be read.
#
# ```
# xz = XzReader.new(file)
# while (piece = xz.read(65536)!) != ""
#   ...
# end
# ```
pub class XzReader
  # The largest dictionary a stream may name unless the caller says
  # otherwise: 64 MiB, what `xz -9` and `xz -9e` write.
  DICT_LIMIT = 67108864_i64
  # The largest a caller may agree to: 1.5 GiB, the most xz's encoder
  # takes, and a ring an Int32 still indexes.
  DICT_MAX = 1610612736_i64

  @core : XzCore

  # *io* gives the compressed stream after *head*, 64 KiB a read, until
  # it answers "". *dict_limit* is the largest dictionary a stream may
  # name, 4 KiB to 1.5 GiB; a stream that names more is an `XzError`
  # before anything is allocated for it. A .xz file is read to the end of
  # its source - streams and the padding between them - so *io* is read
  # until it has no more.
  def initialize(io : IyiIO?, format : XzFormat = XzFormat::Xz, dict_limit : Int64 = DICT_LIMIT, head : String = "")
    unless dict_limit >= 4096_i64 && dict_limit <= DICT_MAX
      raise "XzReader: a dictionary limit is 4 KiB to 1.5 GiB, not #{dict_limit} bytes"
    end
    @core = XzCore.new(format, dict_limit, io, head)
  end

  # Up to *max* decompressed bytes; "" once the stream has ended and
  # everything about it been checked. A read answers as soon as it has
  # bytes and going on would call the source, so it can answer fewer than
  # *max* before the end; and never more than the dictionary at once.
  #
  # A corrupt stream, a check, index or size that does not match, input
  # that ends early, or a dictionary past the limit is an `XzError`, after
  # which every read answers the same error. A block's check is compared
  # after its last byte has been handed out, so the bytes before a bad
  # check have been read by then, as they are from a gzip stream. A *max*
  # below 1 is a panic.
  def read(max : Int32 = 65536) : String | XzError
    @core.read(max)
  end

  # Whether the stream has ended, everything about it been checked, and
  # every byte been read: the next `read` answers "".
  def finished? : Bool
    @core.finished?
  end

  # For `Xz.decompress`.
  protected def core : XzCore
    @core
  end
end

pub struct Xz
  # The bytes *data* decompresses to - every stream of a .xz file, or the
  # one of a .lzma file - or the `XzError` `XzReader` would answer.
  def self.decompress(data : String, format : XzFormat = XzFormat::Xz, dict_limit : Int64 = XzReader::DICT_LIMIT) : String | XzError
    reader = XzReader.new(nil, format, dict_limit, data)
    core = reader.core
    sink = String::Builder.new(data.bytesize < 67108864 ? data.bytesize * 4 + 64 : 268435456)
    core.drain(sink)
    return core.error if core.failed?
    sink.to_s
  end
end
